WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.009 --> 00:00:03.027
- [Woman] No, no it's simple...

00:00:03.027 --> 00:00:05.746
- Ahhhh man
- [Man] Ahhhhh

00:00:05.746 --> 00:00:08.044
(uptempo music)

00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:10.048
- [Auri] 500 million plastic straws

00:00:10.048 --> 00:00:12.228
are used in the US everyday.

00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:14.547
Many of those straws end up in the ocean

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.057
and harm sea life.

00:00:16.057 --> 00:00:17.913
Reports predict that by 2050

00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:22.448
there will be more plastic
in the ocean than fish.

00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:25.031
(cheery music)

00:00:26.423 --> 00:00:28.804
- Hi I'm Auri, and all of those facts

00:00:28.804 --> 00:00:31.325
make me feel so frustrated and hopeless

00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:33.428
and I've been wanting to
do something about this.

00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:35.476
So today I'm going around my office

00:00:35.476 --> 00:00:37.538
and I'm going to be
asking all of my coworkers

00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:39.101
if they'll join me in refusing single

00:00:39.101 --> 00:00:42.551
use plastic straws for a whole week.

00:00:42.551 --> 00:00:44.134
Hello everyone, hi.

00:00:45.319 --> 00:00:46.844
I'm trying to get the whole office

00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:49.205
to not use straws for the next seven days.

00:00:49.205 --> 00:00:50.259
Would you be down to do that?

00:00:50.259 --> 00:00:51.349
- Sure, heck yeah.

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:53.682
- Can I see a show of hands?

00:00:54.523 --> 00:00:55.619
Amazing!

00:00:55.619 --> 00:00:58.693
- Uhhh unfortunately I don't
think I can at the moment

00:00:58.693 --> 00:01:01.675
- I definitely use straws
way too much (laughs)

00:01:01.675 --> 00:01:03.985
- Absolutely, I never
use straws for anything

00:01:03.985 --> 00:01:06.490
- Great, okay so this
goes a step further...

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:08.496
When you're at a restaurant
and you order a drink

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:10.627
you ask for it without a straw

00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:13.627
- Okay what if they give me a straw?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.133
Wow

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:18.082
- Will you pledge to do this
challenge with your signature?

00:01:18.082 --> 00:01:19.332
- Yeah, I'm in.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.447
(upbeat groovy music)

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.948
- Night has fallen and
by the skin of my teeth

00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:31.099
I've managed to collect
a hundred signatures

00:01:31.099 --> 00:01:32.618
from people around the office.

00:01:32.618 --> 00:01:34.133
Let's see how they do.

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:36.595
- I'm at a movie and I can't
have a straw in my soda

00:01:36.595 --> 00:01:40.095
so I'm biting off the end of this red vine

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:43.066
and I'm do it this way.

00:01:45.265 --> 00:01:48.015
(cheerful music)

00:01:54.541 --> 00:01:56.921
- I despise drinking out of glasses

00:01:56.921 --> 00:01:59.104
in public but...
- [Cameraman] Yeah

00:01:59.104 --> 00:02:00.270
We're saving the world.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:01.103
- Sorry

00:02:04.806 --> 00:02:06.337
- Now I know this is a paper cup

00:02:06.337 --> 00:02:08.222
so I don't know if I'm
really actually helping

00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:09.499
the environment by doing this

00:02:09.499 --> 00:02:11.999
but at least there's no straw.

00:02:14.054 --> 00:02:18.547
- No one is here, I'm going
to be looking in the trashes.

00:02:18.547 --> 00:02:21.630
Ooo I see a straw, I see another one.

00:02:24.998 --> 00:02:28.057
I am the straw troll and
the trash does not lie.

00:02:28.057 --> 00:02:29.416
Muahahahahahaha

00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.556
- I already failed um, I just forgot...

00:02:32.556 --> 00:02:35.547
- We don't need straws (laughter)

00:02:35.547 --> 00:02:36.773
- [Camerawoman] We're saving the Earth

00:02:36.773 --> 00:02:37.606
- (bleep)

00:02:37.606 --> 00:02:39.789
- [Camerawoman] One straw at a time

00:02:39.789 --> 00:02:43.278
- I would like a Red Sangria with no straw

00:02:43.278 --> 00:02:45.556
- (speaks in unison) No straw, thank you.

00:02:45.556 --> 00:02:49.139
- I went to Starbucks,
they gave me a straw

00:03:02.046 --> 00:03:03.580
- I'm in a restaurant in Vegas

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:06.844
and I asked for no straw, not
only did you bring a straw...

00:03:06.844 --> 00:03:10.337
Two straws for one
drink now for no reason.

00:03:10.337 --> 00:03:13.911
Like this is way harder than
it should be and I hate it

00:03:13.911 --> 00:03:15.050
like people are dumb.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.508
- Life's not as fun without straws.

00:03:17.508 --> 00:03:22.373
- Thank you so much for
coming it's nice to meet you.

00:03:22.373 --> 00:03:25.025
- Basically there's 500
million plastic straws

00:03:25.025 --> 00:03:27.109
that end up in a landfill every single day

00:03:27.109 --> 00:03:29.832
in the US alone so we
really wanted to offset

00:03:29.832 --> 00:03:32.301
that madness so we
designed this glass straw.

00:03:32.301 --> 00:03:34.133
They had it in the
fifties, we brought it back

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:37.493
and the last 10 to 15 years
we both have been on tour

00:03:37.493 --> 00:03:39.046
competing professionally in snowboarding

00:03:39.046 --> 00:03:40.774
or watching all the crazy things happening

00:03:40.774 --> 00:03:43.213
with our snowpack and climate change

00:03:43.213 --> 00:03:47.380
and our plastic waste channels
is a big part of the problem.

00:03:53.279 --> 00:03:54.796
Alright so I brought a bunch of straws.

00:03:54.796 --> 00:03:56.307
I think we should go pass
them around the office

00:03:56.307 --> 00:03:57.553
see if people get stoked.

00:03:57.553 --> 00:03:58.697
Yeah ?
- Yes, yay

00:03:58.697 --> 00:04:00.570
(together) Cheers

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:02.290
- Goodmorning
- Goodmorning

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.807
- Take your pick, oh yeah

00:04:04.807 --> 00:04:06.140
These are stronger than normal glass.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.599
There are porcelain it's like Pyrex.

00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:08.799
- I'll go with this one.

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:09.838
- [Woman] There you go

00:04:09.838 --> 00:04:12.393
Thank you.
- [Woman] Thank you.

00:04:12.393 --> 00:04:15.143
(cheerful music)

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:18.021
- This straw knew me you know (laughs)

00:04:18.021 --> 00:04:20.271
- Using our reusable straws

00:04:28.792 --> 00:04:30.524
- It's the end of the
challenge how did you do?

00:04:30.524 --> 00:04:31.357
- I did it

00:04:31.357 --> 00:04:32.190
- You did it?

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.731
- I didn't use a straw once.

00:04:33.731 --> 00:04:34.564
- Ah really?

00:04:34.564 --> 00:04:36.024
Well now I feel like a failure.

00:04:36.024 --> 00:04:37.770
I used a straw at least twice.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:39.596
- These are the accidental
straws this week

00:04:39.596 --> 00:04:41.171
and for a hundred people I think

00:04:41.171 --> 00:04:42.933
this amount is pretty good considering

00:04:42.933 --> 00:04:46.600
that most people use
about two straws a day.

00:04:48.278 --> 00:04:51.145
- This week actually turned
out to be super easy.

00:04:51.145 --> 00:04:52.300
- It was really hard.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.548
- From now on, I will be
100 percent straw free.

00:04:56.548 --> 00:04:58.655
- I'm definitely going
back to just getting

00:04:58.655 --> 00:05:00.459
the straws from Starbucks cause

00:05:00.459 --> 00:05:03.304
I probably threw this
away about six times.

00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:04.916
- The beginning of the week I said that

00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:05.973
"Oh I don't use straws".

00:05:05.973 --> 00:05:08.126
You don't realize how much you use straws.

00:05:08.126 --> 00:05:10.382
- This challenge made me more aware

00:05:10.382 --> 00:05:12.660
of how much plastic I was using.

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.549
- It kind of made me realize

00:05:14.549 --> 00:05:16.921
that there are like small
things that you can change

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:19.289
in your own life to
better the environment.

00:05:19.289 --> 00:05:21.642
- I'm so proud of everyone.

00:05:21.642 --> 00:05:24.225
(upbeat music)

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.289
- If you're watching this

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:34.564
and you're literally
still drinking from straws

00:05:34.564 --> 00:05:38.768
you just hate Mother
Earth and it's just fyi.

00:05:38.768 --> 00:05:41.557
- [Auri] I mean he said
it, I did not say it.

00:05:41.557 --> 00:05:43.890
- I didn't lie, truths only.

